-- title:
--   Evaluation at an A-integral place via an 𝒪-section
-- statement:
--   Let $p\ge 5$ be a prime and let $\mathfrak X$ be a `DRModelPackage p`, i.e. the two-chart integral model `DRModel p` of the modular function field of level $p$ over $\mathbb Z$ together with its properness, flatness, integrality and normality data and the identifications $e_0,e_\eta$ of its fibres over $\mathbb Q$ and over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with curve models $M_0$, $M_\eta$. Assume the preimage of the finite chart $\iota_{\mathrm{Fin}}(\top)$ in $M_\eta$ is nonempty and that $M_\eta$ reads the finite chart algebra $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,\mathbb Z$ coefficientwise: for every $a$ in that algebra, the element of `modularFunctionFieldBar p` obtained from the germ of $a$ through `ffEquiv.symm` has Laurent series $\mathrm{coeffEmb}$ of the $q$-expansion of $a$ (hypothesis `hMη`). Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain with maximal ideal generated by $p$, $K$ its fraction field and $\iota_K\colon K\to\overline{\mathbb Q}$ a ring homomorphism, and assume the base change $\mathfrak X_O$ of `DRModel p` to $O$ is integral. Let $x$ be a point of $\mathfrak X_O$ and $\varphi$ a ring homomorphism from the function field of $\mathfrak X_O$ to `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * p)` which sends germs at $x$ of constants $a\in O$ to $\iota_K(a)$ (`hφO`) and which, on the nonempty preimage of the finite chart, reads $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,\mathbb Z$ coefficientwise in the same sense (`hφj`). Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, $k$ a perfect field of characteristic $p$, $\mathrm{red}\colon A\to k$, and let `data`, `hKr`, `hα`, `hβ` be modular polynomial data satisfying the Kronecker congruence at $p$ together with integrality of the two level-raising maps at levels $1,p$; let $P$ be a `PlaceSpecialization` for these data and $R$ a `ProlongationTuple` for $P$. Assume $\iota_K(O)\subseteq A$. Let $e_{\mathrm{Pl}}$ be a bijection between the places of `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * p)` and those of `modularFunctionFieldBar p` which matches valuation subrings and `evalAt`-values on elements with equal Laurent series, and let $V$ be a place of `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * p)` such that $V.\mathrm{ord}(j-a)>0$ for some $a\in A$, where $j$ is `ProlongationTuple.jFun 1 p`. Finally let $t$ be a section of the projection $\mathfrak X_O\to\operatorname{Spec} O$ whose generic point, read over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ through $\iota_K$, is the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-point of $M_\eta$ assigned to $e_{\mathrm{Pl}}(V)$ by `pointEquivPlace` (hypothesis `ht`), and suppose $t$ sends the closed point of $O$ to $x$. Then $x$ lies in the preimage under the first projection of the finite chart $\iota_{\mathrm{Fin}}(\top)$, and for every germ $s$ in the stalk of $\mathfrak X_O$ at that point, $\varphi$ of the image of $s$ in the function field lies in the valuation subring of $V$ and satisfies $V.\mathrm{evalAt}(\varphi(s))=\iota_K(t^{*}s)$, where $t^{*}$ is the induced map `Scheme.stalkClosedPointTo` to $O$.
--
--   This is the integral form of the compatibility between evaluation of modular functions at a place of the geometric generic fibre and pull-back of germs along an $\mathcal O$-valued section of the Deligne–Rapoport model: integrality of $j$ at $V$ relative to $A$, together with $\iota_K(\mathcal O)\subseteq A$, forces the section to meet the $j$-finite chart, so that the chart hypothesis need not be assumed. It feeds the analysis of closed points of the integral model, in particular the identification of sections reducing to a crossing point and the computation of germs of $j$ at such points.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_DRModelPackage_mem_preimage_and_forall_evalAt_eq_stalkClosedPointTo_of_ord_sub_pos.lean

